-- statement:
--   Greedy construction over the first `k` windows.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6Sieve`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Sieve.greedy (d X H : ℕ) (A : ℕ → ℕ) (hA : ∀ i < d, A i + H ≤ X)
--       (hH : sieveBound d X < H) :
--       ∀ k ≤ d, ∃ s : ℕ → ℕ, (∀ i < k, rough (zz d X) (s i) ∧ A i < s i ∧ s i ≤ A i + H) ∧
--         ∀ i < k, ∀ j < k, i ≠ j → Nat.Coprime (s i) (s j)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** J6Sieve: pairwise coprime odd numbers in short windows
--
--   Elementary (Brun pure sieve + greedy) construction: if `d` windows `(A_i, A_i + H]` lie in
--   `(0, X]` and `H > sieveBound d X`, one can choose odd, pairwise coprime `s_i` in them.
--   `sieveBound d X < 2 ^ (4 * (log₂ (4 (d (log₂ X + 1) + 1)) + 2)^2)`.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Part of the Lean formalization of the round-six κ-improvement (integer-multiplication-kappa campaign, target `IntMul.Kappa.jain_round6_framework`). The statement is copied verbatim from the Lean development; the platform node carries the same declaration name. Definitions it mentions live in the `IntMul_Kappa_R6_Defs*` bundles (on top of the published κ bundles `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs*`).
